.TH INETGATEWAY 1 "November 2026" "InetGateway" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
inetgateway \- offline packet viewer with a per-application dashboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B inetgateway
[\fB\-\-demo\fR] [\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B InetGateway
is a graphical, Wireshark-style traffic viewer. It captures what reaches this
computer, decodes it, and groups it by program and service on a dashboard.
It never decrypts traffic, never blocks or changes anything, and makes no
network connections unless the optional VirusTotal lookups are enabled in the
Threat Intel tab.
.PP
Live capture needs root or the CAP_NET_RAW capability, for example:
.PP
.RS
sudo \-E inetgateway
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Show clearly labelled synthetic traffic (for trying the interface; nothing is captured).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/InetGateway/config.json
Settings. The optional VirusTotal key and lookup cache are stored next to it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.I /usr/share/doc/inetgateway/
